    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d281">

                <pb facs="0578" n="544" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v15p1/pg544"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">FE files, lot 55 D 128: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commander in Chief, Far East (Clark) to the
                        President</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d281-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top
                            secret<lb/>operational immediate</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-09-27T14:19:00+09:00">September 27, 1952—2:19
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>C 55891. Ref urmsg 261925Z.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d281-f2"/></p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>I have recd from the JCS the course of action to be fold at Pan Mun Jom as
                        approved by you. I wish to inform you that the initial statement will be
                        made by the UNC Armistice Delegation at the meeting on 28 Sep 1952,<anchor
                            n="3" xml:id="d281-f3"/> and that it will be presented with the utmost
                        firmness and without subsequent debate. The Delegation will further insist
                        that the Communists reply to our just and honorable proposal at a meeting of
                        the Armistice Delegations on or about 8 Oct 1952.</item>
                    <pb facs="0579" n="545" xml:id="pg545"/>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>If at the later meeting the Communists reject our proposal, the UNC
                        Armistice Delegation will make it unmistakably clear to the Communists that
                        having made a proposal which would result in a fair and just armistice and
                        the Communists having rejected same that we do declare an indefinite recess
                        of the meetings. Concurrent with declaring the indefinite recess of the
                        armistice meetings, the Delegation will inform the Communists that the UNC
                        Delegation is willing to reconvene armistice sessions at any time that the
                        Communists express a willingness to accept our proposal.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>I wish to assure you that throughout this coming period the mil pressure
                        will not be lessened. Every effort will be made to increase the pressure,
                        principally by air action.</item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d281-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d281-f1-content">
                <p>This telegram marked “personal from General Clark” was repeated to the JCS and
                    the Secretary of Defense for their information.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d281-f2" n="2" xml:id="d281-f2-content">
                <p><hi rendition="#italic"><ref target="#d281">Supra</ref></hi>; a note on the
                    source text indicated that telegrams 261925Z and 262005Z were identical.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d281-f3" n="3" xml:id="d281-f3-content">
                <p>For a text of the statement, see telegram Z 23092, <hi rendition="#italic"><ref
                            target="#d282">infra</ref></hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
